Emmett Till was a 14-year-old African American boy who was brutally murdered in 1955 in Mississippi, United States.&nbsp;
Till’s death became a symbol of the racial violence and injustice that African Americans faced in the segregated South.
On August 24, 1955, Till arrived from Chicago in Money, Mississippi, to visit his family. A few days later, he and some friends went to a local grocery store, where Till allegedly whistled at a white woman named Carolyn Bryant.
